<article class="env-definition" id="08WQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08WQ">Definition <span data-tag="08WQ">35.4.9</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Define the contravariant functor <em>$C$</em> $ : \text{Mod}_ R \to \text{Mod}_ R$ by setting </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  C(M) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\textit{Ab}}(M, \mathbf{Q}/\mathbf{Z}),  \]
</div>
  <p> with the $R$-action on $C(M)$ given by $rf(s) = f(rs)$. </p>
</article>